  "prefLabel": "Odb 207.01 Request for Rule Explanation",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Odb 207.01 Request for Rule Explanation.\n\n(a) Any person may request, at any time before 30 days after the final adoption of the rule, that the board issue an explanation of a rule by filing an original and one copy of the request.\n\n(b) The request shall include:\n\n(1) The chapter, part or section, or paragraph, by alphanumeric code, of the rule(s), statutory provision(s), or order(s) which is the subject of the request; and\n\n(2) Any other information as the person filing the petition deems pertinent and relevant, including attachments, illustrations, and other written documents.\n\nSource. #8490-B, eff 11-22-05; ss by #10481, eff 12-3-13; ss by #12941, eff 12-15-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/odb100-600.html"
